    <summary>Shows which of your Claude Code and Codex sessions is waiting for you.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[A strip of cards on the edge of your screen that shows which of your Claude Code and Codex sessions is waiting for you. One card per Alacritty window. Click a card, land in that window.

![NodLight](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/jnury/NodLight@main/docs/images/deck.png)

## Features

- **One card per session**: window title, a `claude` or `codex` badge, the status with how long it has been in it, and the project folder.
- **Status at a glance**: orange with a slow blink when a session waits for you, green while it works, grey when idle.
- **Resource use per session**: CPU, memory and disk/network I/O of everything running under that window.
- **Click to focus**: the window comes to the front, restored if it was minimised.
- **Taskbar button** to show or hide the strip, with a count of waiting, working and idle sessions.
- **Follows Windows** light or dark mode and accent colour.

## Notes

- Needs Windows 11 and [Alacritty](https://alacritty.org/). The .NET 10 Desktop Runtime is installed as a dependency.
- This package installs NodLight for all users, under `C:\Program Files\NodLight`.
- On first start NodLight offers to add its hooks to Claude Code and Codex. Run `/hooks` in Codex once to trust them.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/jnury/NodLight/releases/tag/v1.0.2</releaseNotes>
